        "text": "Italian media reported that the theme in the video is as an attempt to promote racism and anti-Semitation by the Italian authorities. Below is a video showing the man being snapped by police while holding a gun. Apparently a police officer, Angelio Pilosira, was arrested. It’s still not clear which theme in the video received most attention, but we’re happy to see the color and different hues in the video being strong enough to receive many positive reviews. Where’s Your Board? Photo by Eric Bowts, October 27, 2013 Development by Alcara and Kristica Begum Alcara and Kristica developed a player-driven board game called DarkS, a board-driven virtual reality gaming game developed by Kristica Begum and Alcara Begum. I just started my career as a developer and was fascinated with virtual reality gaming, but when I first joined in, I was really obsessed with board games. I joined up with them to develop a player-driven board game that allows you to play on a mobile device to fit your needs and that is ready for play on a mobile device, as a computer or in a virtual reality game. For you who haven’t yet read the official development report for the project or haven’t yet been familiar with it, I’d really love to hear more about you, as I don’t know what else I can possibly do with a virtual reality board. If you have any other ideas for virtual reality gaming or have something to share, feel free to contact me in the comments section. About Genali The Genella is an absolutely awesome game where you head on a large European island and you find yourself with a small group of aliens living on the island's surface. You find yourself trapped in a mysterious dark place and secretly trying to save the rest of the universe. This device, also known as the Darking Spacer, places you in the world's virtual reality dynamosphere where three satellites are told to move at a temperature of around 80 degrees F. This will take you to a strange location codenamed the \"pre-European Ocean\". It's a completely different game combining awesome combat effects, great gameplay, advanced mapping and brand new features to take you on a mysterious and alien journey through Europe's big islands and strange worlds. This game is developed by Alcara and Kristica Begum in their latest film DarkS. About Board Games In an action game played in a dark place called the Vergelan Ocean, the developers want to create an exciting board game to play with that lets you push satellites into a dark place, move them above the Earth's surface and then save them. This will be a classic version of a board game called the Rain Spacer. If you don't believe it's a classic version of the iPhone 6X, don't take it too seriously if you don't play it by hand. About Genali The board project was started with the collaboration of Genali Board Games, a group of developers from University of London, University of Oxford and the University of Nottingham. They developed a board game called Vgenali and a Rain Spacer for PlayStation One. Now on the PlayStation 4 PC, the team is developing a new board game that lets you push your satellites into the ocean. They want to get the game ready for play through a detailed development process. The team has been working with them on this project since 2009. After kicking off the project back in Hong Kong in 2010, the team decided to complete some initial demos to get the game ready for play. After that, the team is still working on getting the game ready for the PlayStation 4 PC, with a few months to be done though. Once all is done, the developers are back to work on the project. They will be travelling to Hong Kong for the next year to set up a military base in the Vergelan Ocean which will be used to carry out space missions, as well as to defend the planets. To perform this mission, the player must set up a satellite to determine if this base is going to be capable of sending out the satellites. What's amazing about the project is the amazing experience in the Vergelan Ocean which not only gives them an glimpse into the ship and its universe, it also gives them a glimpse of where they come from so they know what's going on a space mission. The goal is to give a player a glimpse of the universe and show them how fun it is to travel through this dark place and give them a chance to learn more about the universe so they don't be afraid of traveling through the depths of other planets."
