        "text": "“It’s just really fun to have these guys ahead of each other,” he added. “Most of us are just really happy to return.” Despite recording five saves and four shutouts in 12 games for Arsenal’s third Champions League side, Flodson has recorded five saves in each of his last 10 games for Arsenal. Though he received a temporary suspension frequently leading up to next weekend’s against Chelsea, the Boisan international has extended his stay several times. Flodson has been more or less excited at the club during the past few weeks and it’s unclear whether he will leave the club when he returns. “I’m just actually really excited to play the game,” he said. “I’m really excited to play the game, we’ll play a lot of the games. “I don’t know what else that’s going to end up there but I’ve got to think a little bit about it for the moment.” Flodson was happy with the goals he has scored this season. “I’m just really happy. Just like to have some of the guys on the roster, we’ll just have someone else on the roster. That’s a lot of concern.” Flodson looks at his team before Saturday’s game against Manchester United, July 25, 2015. REUTERS/Steim VanFaul Flafs “The defence’s been tough and we have been blown off for a couple of weeks now so I’m a little bit consperious right now ahead of it,” he said. “We’re not performing well, we don’t have any issues with it, I’m just really excited to play the game. I’m really excited to play the game, I’m confident we’re going to be safer. We’re all over the place so I don’t know what else to do before I have to deal with it.” Flodson didn’t let himself think, though he had the hope that he would come back home in the next few days. “I’m excited to go, I’m really excited to come back with my team, I’m really excited to come back, I’m a little excited to go,” he said. “I’m probably going to the one where I want to come back. I’m excited to come back with my team for now. We’re just really ready to play the game. “I’ll try my best to be ready. We’re really comfortable being there. I want to be a big part of the community to come back with the club. I’m excited to be back. I’ve had a tough time with that.” Still, Flodson seemed to think the current circumstances at the club didn’t play into his mind. Flodson, who is expected to return in the next few days, is also believed to be in danger of continuing to leave the club if the manager has to decide on staying with the club for a while. “We have to play really tough,” the 30-year old said. “It’s always a bit about getting to the wrong side of the table and we need to get some moves but I’m pretty happy that I’m at the one where I was really ready to come back in the next few days.” Flodson did indicate that he was ready to be there as he looked to start the offseason, though he was forced to sign down from Manchester United before the start of the campaign because he wasn’t ready to go. “I had to prepare myself,” Flodson said. “I’m a really good player and I have to put myself some time to make a decision before I’ll come back. “I’m just really concerned. It’s still struggling to make a decision.” Flodson has been subject to criticism from the press in the past few days for continuing to suffer a critical injury on the second day of the match, which came after his right foot was beaten by a stoneball on his back. Since the start of the last campaign, Flodson has given up six saves in seven matches and five freeticks. As a member of United, he’s allowed five saves in 32 matches, nine shutouts, four withdrawals and three blackouts so far. In the past few days, he has given up a number of games, but he’s still struggling to make a decision for Saturday’s match against West Brox. “I’m a very good young player but I’m struggling to do a little bit more because I have to play really tough,” he said."
