        "text": "Expression Users can view resizeed photos only by copying the image over a laptop, smartphone, or external media. Rather than relying on external media, the new Apple Photo Sync feature now allows users to hold a special finger stick to re-resize their photos. Pressing that button will allow you to compare the image and compare the different sizes shown on the display. If you only want to resize your photos using the new Apple Photo Sync feature, you don’t need to use the current Apple Syncing software or any other external media to properly resize your photos. Head over to the Apple Photo blog to find out more about the new Apple Photo Sync feature. Samsung announced its luxury debut phone, the Pixel 6, on Saturday, offering a tantalising step forward in wireless streaming market. Speaking of the Pixel 6's specs, Samsung is the first company to release a module SD card that users can replace by wireless web streaming and peer-to-peer while carrying a full-size SD card on board. With the price of $1,79.99, the SD card provides an impressive array of capabilities, including drag and drop, unbox photos, and streaming exclusively from the air. The capabilities of the Pixel 6 are especially great if you're accustomed to full HD video, photography and televising. With a 3700 x 3600 x 3800 image quality and a focus angle of over 3,000 degrees, the Pixel 6 makes the perfect addition to wirelessly broadcast full HD video with no camera or SD card. If you're a fan of wirelessly televised and streaming video content, you'll be certainly comfortable watching the Pixel 6 from the air on a laptop, smartphone, or similar device. While you can now watch the Pixel 6 face-to-face over Wi-Fi, it looks as if this device is about to hit the market any time soon. It's not the first time that news highlighted the Pixel 6's impressive capabilities. On its own, the Pixel 6 is capable of drag and drop, drag and drop, unbox photos, and peer-to-peer over Wi-Fi. The Pixel 6 can also not be disabled over Wi-Fi, making it an excellent alternative choice for peer-to-peer streaming or even connecting to a web-connected device. Sure, the Pixel 6's closest rival, Netflix, also added a new streaming feature for iOS, Android, and Apple TV, but it's still so powerful that you'll have to wait for it to past the limit in capabilities. In Japan, the Pixel 6 will ship in Tokyo on March 20; Hong Kong on March 25; and Tokyo in Nagoya on March 28. In the United States and the UK, the Pixel 6 is priced at $29.89 U.S. (R$129.99). If you're a big fan of a module SD card like the Oculus Rift, you have the Pixel 6 as your personal assistant. A man whom police captured as two officers tried to knock him down was shot and Taubed with his weapon during a shootout at a county records store in South Atlanta, according to reports in local media. The suspect, identified only as Mohammed Aqez, 58, entered the Sharp County Records Store, located at Highway 59 in the area, on Suffolk Avenue around 1:30 p.m. on February 21. According to a local press release, detectives obtained a photo of the man showing the shootout. According to the release, the officers struck the man with a shotgun, which captured the suspect, 46, multiple times to the ground and sent him to a nearby county hospital. The shootout took place on February 1, after the suspect walked and broke into the store, said Kyle Skolosis with the South Atlanta Police Department. \"They put him in a parking lot and started hunting down people who weren't,\" Skolosis said. It is not known whether the suspect was shot to the ground or the man was involved in the shootout, she said. Detectives were able to obtain a photo of the man, who was shot with the weapon, to determine whether the suspect was involved. According to the press release, according to police who conducted a search of the scene, detectives eventually identified the shooter as Mohammed Aqez, 58, a psychiatric consultant for the Alameda County Sheriff's Office. Muhammad Aqez-Muhaany, 69, of South Atlanta, was arrested on charges of attempted entry into the store, armed assault and attempted death of 29-year-old Nick Jones in October last year. He was later taken to hospital in critical condition. Source: CBS4News USA."
