        "id": "s-688d0c4ea865c3c3d0627d08",
        "sourceId": 359,
        "text": "The Crimean international is expected to sign a contract before the end of January and can score another goal for Celtic before the end of the season. However, despite failing to quite secure the Champions League final in just the two weeks since he was signed from Real Madrid, he has improved significantly overall than he did at Trafford. However, last season Sergio Espaldin did not manage nearly 10 goals so far and also netted only eight goals in the Fifa Cup final, helping him add momentum to his attacking and helping the team reach the top of the top 10. Gabriel Mkinho (serious tendon injury) Related Sports Gabriel Mkinho's career at United has been generally left relatively tense, plagued by a tendon injury and the prospect of a return to the squad. The former Arsenal midfielder has been an consistent top 10 striker since arriving at United and netted six goals in United's win at Old Trafford at the end of January, a beautiful moment in his career. However, the impressive loss of Gabriel Mkinho is often labeled to be the biggest disappointment of his time at United as he is viewed as one of the most talented football players at the club. He has been called upon to play alongside Mauriciio Bozico while players are beginning to put their pressure on him and since the start of last year's Cup final Mkinho has suffered a tendon injury. 2 Sam Couppe from Manchester United (£8.6m) The Spanish left-back has been in the middle of a busy season, following Hutford's impressive two-goal win at Wembley on 21 January. He has been burdened with a number of problems on the pitch; however, short term injuries have limited his development for much of this season. As the youngest striker for much of his career he has been extremely inconsistent on the pitch and on his own, particularly off the bench. His best start has come in the 2-0 draw with Chelsea City in November, when he was replaced by a younger 19-year-old just before the end of the season. At 27 years old, Couppe has had an astonishing amount of time to improve from the outset. In recent months he has proven to be well ahead of the top 10 rankings, where he will need to score 10 more goals to secure his first top three spot. Couppe's time at United has unsurprisingly been a fairly solid season so far, with United's top ten strikers scoring 11 goals during that time – well above the maximum of nine. 1 Luis Costa from Costa (£3.5m) The biggest moment of Costa's career came in Costa's late draw with Real Madrid at the end of last season. Although United did score a handful of goals in the build-up to its Champions League final, Costa went on to net one of those in a 3-0 win at Trafford. The player has scored six goals and two assists for United, which proved to be a key milestone in his first team campaign. The player struggled with all-around keeper Luis Suarez in the final 15 minutes at United, costping short an improbable win over rivals Real Madrid before scoring a short-range goal to claim second place in the top table. Although Costa is fighting for a solid finish in the third round of the table against Liverpool, the club will have been hesitant to put a chance on the Spanish midfielder near the end of this season. Although rare for a player with impressive attacking skills, Costa has also proven to be a powerful attacking force which has left him short of an ideal for this home season. It is hard to imagine a player like Costa making a major impact during his time at United, although we are very close to seeing him work hard to secure a decisive run to the European Champions League. A £3 million signing from Manchester United, the left-back has struggled in just 120 Premier League games for his home club Old Trafford and consistently sits in the league's top 10 – only second in the table behind Team Real. However, he was eventually rewarded with a stunning pay-off in a powerful 2-0 win over Huton. The Colombia international scored 11 of the 14 goals to help United reach their 178.5-goal total and advance to their first European League title. Although his injuries have been a contributing concern – particularly with Michael Benhazi undergoing treatment to play for the UAE Emirates – there is relatively little chance he could return to full form at the club. This season has proved to be an exciting one for the 41-year-old; however, we are very close to seeing him make his full impact at United this campaign."
