        "sourceId": 619,
        "text": "Samsung is poised to reveal a new unit known as the Tiz 2, which will power a variety of new devices, particularly the Galaxy Note 4. The Tiz 2 is now available for purchase, with prices from $49 on Samsung's pre-ordered XL to $49 on the General Access XL by the end of 2017. With no launch date previously set for Samsung's flagship unit, this looks to be the first time any new device may come to market, as it will be available for download on Samsung's XL mobile and Android phones. Samsung began matching prices on the XL last year against those on the XHL last August, and the company recently released a prototype of its XHL version for use on its new Galaxy Note 4. The XHL version is available on Samsung's top-end phones, and will reportedly be unavailable until early 2017. Reuters first reported that Samsung is planning to start manufacturing on the Tiz 2, another larger and higher-performance (7.5-inch) Galaxy Note 4 device which debuted on the iPhone one week ago. While Reuters reports the unit will start manufacturing in July, performance and quality are being praised on the Tiz 2, which are being offered for purchase in advance of the Samsung launch. The Tiz 2 is a7.5-inch tall device that sits approximately 6.5 inches by 7.5 inches across. The device is in contrast to the Galaxy Note 4, which debuted at the launch event in Hong Kong last month. Like several other Samsung devices recently showcased on the company's Tiz 2 website, the Galaxy Note 4 will sport a contrasting 3D display in time for the device's launch on June 9, 2017. Though whose display will be similar to that depicted on the Galaxy Note 4, the Tiz 2's display will have a more futuristic look, as reflected by shortened battery life, making access to touch and button more convenient, as well as a much brighter screen seen on many other Samsung devices. The Galaxy Note 4 will display the same brand new features first seen in Samsung's June showcase, although they will go on sale in 2017. In addition to extended battery life, improved touch control and on-and-off features seen on the Galaxy Note 4, the Samsung Tiz will boast a compact touch controller enabling the liberation of screen control as shown in the picture to right of its Tiz version. 50 Meter Ben Zhang Development Of The 50 Meter Ben Zhang Building in Waning. The city has successfully completed urban construction of the 50meter building, an eight-story site located between Wu and Zhang drives on the Chinese coast. Developers believe the site will be a mixed-use complex that adds an estimated height of 400 square meters of ground-floor housing. Suxi Wu Drive. This development, located at the intersection of Wu Drive and Ky Wu Park, would improve urban development with a significant impact on the Foster Island neighborhood. Located at the intersection of Wu Drive, the proposed development will add 700 square meters of retail area, porchs and 80 or 101 square meters of housing to the city's Upper East Side neighborhood. Chinese Central Government Agency. Models for the project will add 800 square meters of office space, 580 square meters of residential space and 32.29 square meters of retail area. Suxi Wu Drive. This proposed development, which includes 349,000 square meters of housing, will include 617 apartments with a predicted height of 700 square meters. It will also add construction capacity for a total area of 31,521 square meters that will house an estimated 56,000 square meters of residents. Suxi Wu Center. This site, located at the intersection of Wu Drive, will be developed as a mixed-use, 1 trillion yuan annual complex on Foster Island. With the removal of a parking space and overhauled street architecture, the site forms the basis of a successful urban neighborhood in central China with a per-capita income of $387,562. Ky Wu Park Waning. The proposed development will add 2.8 trillion yuan ($40M) of construction capacity for a total area of 1,700 square meters. It will also house a predicted 73,000 square meters of residents. Ky Wu Park Downtown.Located at the intersection of Wu Drive, this development will add 166 square meters of office space. Models for the project include to overhaul the site, introducing new affordable features. The initial construction phase and predicted 10-year construction period will be complete by spring of 2017. Kyji Muiqong County And Kyji Muiqong County with a population of about 145,000, the development includes an expected 164 apartments, 231 offices and 95 square meters of housing. Between Waning and Fuqhi County, the proposed development will add 81 square meters (3.6M) housing."
