        "id": "s-cb02c92397f4c74327468e45",
        "sourceId": 623,
        "text": "China has so far invested about $500m in the development of a miniballistic missile system. The Titan destroyer, which has four cruise missiles, received a round of purchases in 2009 from Beijing at a price of around $200m. The Titan destroyer is part of what was seen as a deterrence for China's nuclear program. The country last week agreed to cooperate with Russia for a militarised 22-caliber miniballistic missile. Both China and Russia did not respond to a request for comment. KAHUL (AP) -- U.S. officials are working with American partners in Kabul to ensure safety of suspected al Qaeda affiliates following a strike on the mosque on Friday, Bin Abdul said in his Facebook post. Pakistani security forces said they had arrested Ali Mustafa Bin Abdul at his home in Altis Falls, Pakistan. Bin Abdul is a al Qaeda affiliate from Afghanistan. In his Facebook post, Bin Abdul said the United States was working with Pakistani authorities to ensure the forces there took appropriate measures against a terror invading there. But speaking to reporters, Bin Abdul said he did not consider the attack a terror. The strike took place at the Muhammad Ali Yasainha mosque in Kabul, a building which functions as a base for U.S. military forces. Known as 'Tyrants' \"Everyone who commits this horrific act, so-called terrorism, should express their heartfelt support and allegiances to these terrorists,\" Bin Abdul said. \"It's not a justified terror,\" he added. A U.S. embassy spokesperson said no person had been arrested in the strike. The attack on the New York mosque took place about 11 a.m. Friday. Three enemy warheads were fired at the mosque, officials said. The Pentagon identified the attackers as members of the Sunni-based al Qaeda affiliate based in Yemen. It said they were members of a wider network of Sunni Muslims affiliated with the United States. \"Pakistani men and women, with the backing of the American people, stand together against the deadlywing of (known as) al Qaeda,\" Pakistani Foreign Minister Ayatollah Ali Khasolini said in a statement on Saturday. \"We will not surrender to any tyrants operating within our country. We will work with all American partners to combat this threat.\" Pakistani police said they had offered additional assistance in carrying out measures against suspected members of al Qaeda. Bookmark with: Delicious Digg reddit Facebook StumbleUpon What are these? E-mail this to a friend Printable version The battle for an iPad may not be officially over, but if you’re looking to get your hands on an easy-to-find iPad, Apple Pays will roll out a 30-day delivery discount this fall for users with Apple accounts. The discount will go into effect every month, so basically if you decide to make a purchase, you’ll only want to save $200 off the device. If you have an Apple account, Apple Pays is also offering an extension of this 30-day delivery discount to people who have not boughtd an Apple device since 1995. Just... 30 days! Once the extension is approved in fall 2018, the discount will save another $200 off the device for people buying the iPad. It is a pretty popular discount, and Apple has long sought to offer it to users who hadn’t bought an iPad since 1995. For now, Apple Pays is also offering a discount to users who hadn’t bought an Apple device since 1995. In addition, they plan to unveil an Apple TV release in the next few weeks. In recent months, we've been hearing that Apple is nearing to give up its most expensive rival, the Apple iPhone X, but it's also just too soon to see Apple cash in on the low-cost rival. LeTimes has revealed that Apple's new iPhone will start at $500, with a starting price of $649. These aren't the first reports of an Apple-made iPhone X device. For instance, the iPhone X will retail around $800 after launch, targeting entry-level users. The iPhone X will also feature twin-core storage; it's due for launch in late September this year. iPhone X will also include wireless charging. The device will run a 3.5GHz GeForce GPU, and should represent Apple's best shot at a new consumer experience. But after watching the first glimpse of the Apple iPhone X, one can get a good sense that Apple is behind the bar when it comes to other expensive devices, like the upcoming Apple TV X 2. Indeed, the price of the new iPhone is around $2699,000."
