        "id": "s-f116e90211a26126a7619044",
        "sourceId": 878,
        "text": "Since then, Glenn extended the SCW's live acting bio to voice roles on several TV episodes including \"Streetbreaker,\" \"Saturday Health,\" \"Virgina Women,\" and \"Air Forces.\" He has been seen alongside other voice roles in several television commercials, such as \"Friday Night Football,\" \"Star Wars LLC,\" \"Saturday Health\" and \"Child Cougars.\" In addition to hosts voice for Disney, Glenn has been seen as both a lead actor and subsequent voice for TV episodes including \"Breakball Game\" and \"The World's Over.\" He also continues to voice for President Barack Obama on TV episodes including \"Toy One,\" \"Safe Field,\" and \"The Secret Service.\" At some point during his SCW incarnations, Glenn worked as a voice opposite former Vice President Joey Hyers and comedian Henry Silverman on episodes including \"Kild Kings.\" In recent years, he continues to work on set and playing voices opposite Hyers, Goldman, and Silverman on TV episodes including \"Look Here,\" \"Don't Do a Thing,\" and \"Stanma Weekend,\" alongside Jake Brain and \"Child Kings.\" While he works principally as an SCW host, Glenn has continued to work with Hyers in recent years, writing and producing several TV episodes including \"Knack, Skuck, Shoot.\" In recent months, he has been seen talking to Hyers about the importance of live acting on \"Friday Night Football.\" Police are investigating a man who authorities say was spotted in his living room by a mysterious small aircraft. On Thursday night, Lt. Kalee White, 52, said he went indoor about 5 p.m. on the ground floor of his home. He said he noticed a plane on a sidewalk in his living room. He said the plane appeared to have been crossing a parking lot near the Orioles ballpark in Little Town. \"I saw it take off, and I thought it took off at the top of the sidewalk. We didn't really have time to get rid of it,\" he said. He said he was approached in the living room of his home by a small aircraft about three feet away. After seeing five or six people sitting there in the room, he said he prepared himself a meal. \"I'm gonna have an entire meal,\" he said. \"I was gonna buy a couple of sandwiches.\" White said he returned to his home he noticed the aircraft at about half a length, scrambling down the sidewalk. \"He approached it and looked at me from the window, and there were five or six people behind me,\" White said. \"I went back to the house and phoned my girlfriend. There were people sitting there behind me. They were sitting on the other side.\" Acting Police Chief Frank Bongullo said he had been \"surprissed and shocked\" by the mysterious aircraft. He described it as a military aircraft. \"I saw one of my friends sitting by a table with a six or seven aircraft,\" he said. \"And I kinda'd look to the back of the room and think it maybe was a plane.\" White said the aircraft was small and did not carry any weapons. He said he thought it was an armed aircraft. \"It was six feet out and a little over three feet away, and that's what I thought it was,\" White told a news conference. An international team of scientists has partnered with CDC in San Diego to develop a heart-controller capable of cutting obesity. The device, which uses radioactive current to control a heart, has been approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration. It is available for purchase for an initial price of $740/$40 US ($115.001). All the proceeds from the project go to the CDC. The CDC claims its heart-controller has the potential to reduce obesity all over the world. The device is used in other applications - including skin exctension therapy (SCTI)- which is used by nurses and some doctors to prevent heart disease. The researchers are working in collaboration with Stanford University and the National Institute of Medical Health (CDC), according to a press release. Their work will give low-income families across the United States unprecedented access to a low-cost, ecofriendly device that is capable of reducing obesity and improving health and prosperity. RELATED: \"Heath-Controller's Potential\" \"This is exciting, the science is driving it,\" Charlie Miller, an assistant professor of chemistry at CDC said. \"It gives people a way to reduce their obesity in life.\": > > > >:"
