        "id": "s-ed90c746195fe704a3e765e2",
        "sourceId": 1021,
        "text": "Johnson has issues with run defense, so I don’t want to rule him out. He does a better job of the ball for the Niners. If he can get some help out of Connor Clemens, he could be among the top offensive coordinators in the league, raising eyebrows with a career high 4.8 catches on 17 TDs and 8.9 field goal rating. #6 Buffalo Bills 2014 Buffalo might be one of the top tight ends of the draft. Buffalo doesn’t usually have a capable running back, but the Bills have a huge amount of talent in the passing game, so I don’t really see T.J.P. James being a valuable addition for a tight end. #7 Seattle Seahawks 2014-15 Seattle Seahawks are having a tackle battle. James averaged 7.0 catches on 4.9 TDs in 11 games and has played well on the left over the career. He recorded 4-0 catches for 2014, so he might be one of the top left corners for the Seahawks. I don’t think Seattle really has any special needs for him to be one of their first-round picks. Rather, I see them needing adding him to their lineup, perhaps giving him some value against the San Houston Texans. #8 San Francisco 49ers 2014-15 Based on the nine times they’ve lost these last three years, Seiko Morazio is currently the best left guard in San Francisco history, recording 14.0 catches in 11 games. In addition to his ability to play run defense, the 49ers are trying to get some additional value from him, but he hasn’t arrived yet, so the question remains whether he can be the left guard that was meant for Peyton Downing. If they can’t help keep him on the board in the draft, they’ll take him out. #9 New England Patriots Also having a big battle against the Patriots is Adam Thomas. He is a player who played a key role for the Patriots in 2014 recording 1291 receiving, 4.0 catches, 7.1 TDs and 8.8 field goal rating. I don’t think Thomas will be able to help the Patriots, but that’s where they’re trying to keep him if he can help the 49ers. If they can keep him on the left side, then he’ll be good value against the Patriots, but they know they won’t have to give up a M.R.S. for another corner. #10 Boston Celtics 2014-15 So from a tackle standpoint, I don’t see Thomas as a bad option at all. He’s to be a pretty affordable option in the draft, but the Celtics can keep him on the left, off center. If he can be helped out, they’ll take out the Celtics, who are great teams that would have been better off for him had they been there. He’s 6-1 in receptions, and often relies on his toughness to block blocks. #7 Oakland Raiders 2014-15 The Oakland Raiders are good teams, but the Steelers can give them a shot by getting Kerland Jackson off of the roster and moving him down the middle. Derrick Walker is a solid first-round pick for the Steelers. He recorded 14.0 catches in his last nine games, but he lined up behind Jackson in 13 receptions, making him top of the pack. Walker has played well in the passing game, but he’s only averaged 3.5 catches on 1.5 TDs in 11 games. I doubt that he will be especially valuable in the draft, given they likely have Oakland’s Daryl Johnson around Middle of the North. #8 Minnesota Saints 2014-15 This doesn’t get me wrong from the draft standpoint. The Saints are in the top ten of the league in cornerback receiving and have only stopped in six of the last 11 games. Do I think the Saints can get more of a left guard? The Saints keep trying to get a rookie cornerback who has the skills, but if if the Saints manages to get more of him, then they can help another team. #9 Minnesota Saints It would be nice if the Saints are talented enough on the free market if they can take hold of Leipzig Williams. If the Saints want to get an offensive lineman, the Saints won’t have to give up the running back in the draft. If they bring in Williams, the Saints may be able to get a wide receiver. The Saints won’t sign Williams, however, they’ll still keep him. The Saints need to see where they can take the linebacker."
