        "sourceId": 370,
        "text": "Astronomers from the Universities of Virginia, Clemson and Columbia University suggest that the explosion could have been directly triggered by a smaller sphere. The video shows an image of a planet flying outwards from the sun that appears to drop off its side. The planet gravitates naturally toward Earth, then fluctuates vertically as it swungs away. They suggest that the explosion could have been caused by a smaller sphere, or an increase in the sensitivity to magnetic fields. Astrologists from the Universities of Virginia, Clemson and Columbia University have previously suggested that the explosion could have been triggered by a smaller sphere. Their findings, published online Thursday in The New York Times, offer a new perspective on how the explosion could have been caused by a sphere that was slightly smaller. The planet, rather than a yellow sphere, fronted in a blue circle. It flew away from the sun, and it moved away into a slew of red circles. If the planet had been slightly smaller, the planet would move into a red circle, and it would move beyond its natural limits toward the rest of the universe. However, for the first time in recent memory, this could have been caused by a smaller sphere. \"Another possibility is that this could be a result of a smaller sphere, or an increase in the sensitivity to magnetic fields that would cause a collision to occur,\" MIT physicist David Hassan, who was part of the research team, told The New York Times. \"However, it's possible that this could have been caused by a smaller sphere,\" Hassan added. The scientists suggest that the explosion's rhythms could have been a result of a sun effect. In simple terms, the sun is a stream of light that emerges from inside the sun and sits on the Earth's surface. However, the sun's movement varies depending on the circumstances. For example, when the sun enters the Earth, the sun gradually warms up and emits more energy. The sun gradually slows, and this energy gradually warms up, which is slowing the sun's movement across the magnetic spectrum. \"From the moment of the explosion, the sun's angularity will vary from stable to inangular, so we need to monitor the sun's freedom of movement across the magnetic spectrum at the moment of explosion,\" said Lisa Papten, president of CBSNews.com. The research is published online by the National Academy of Sciences. It can be accessed from CBSNews.com. A gunman has been charged after he shot and killed two people at a local nightclub in Maricopa, Texas A gunman has been charged after he shot and killed two people at a local nightclub in Maricopa, Texas (AP Photo/Alex Addico) Police said the shooting occurred in the 1500 block of Vanderholoe Street in Maricopa at about 5:50 a.m. on Thursday night. Police said the shooter, a 29-year-old male, in a black suit and wearing blue glasses, was sitting in his car and seated on a table in the corner when he was gunshot. Police said at the time that a gunman had shot three people, including a male shooter and a female shooter. Each victim was rushed to a nearby hospital, police said. Both victims were taken by the ambulance to University General Hospital. The male, in a black T-shirt and wearing blue glasses, while the female shooter, in a black suit and wearing blue glasses, has been taken into critical care with a life-threatening injury. The shooting was treated at University General Hospital and was seeing a doctor, police said. Both victims were taken to University General Hospital in critical condition. The victims, male and female, were not seen in the area at the time of the shooting, press releases state. Police would not comment on the identities of the two victims, and it was unclear if a photo of the suspects was released at this time. All The suspects, who were male and female, were not seen in the area at the time of the shooting, police said. Press releases state that all of the victims were taken to University General Hospital. The four The suspects were taken to University General Hospital in critical condition. The other four victims were seen at the time that the shooting first went off, press releases state. \"By sending a clear message of solidarity to a community that has been plagued by persistent gun violence, we hope to ensure that law enforcement has the best information available to deal with this tragic time,\" New York Mayor Michael Bloomberg said in a statement."
