        "text": "PLAENCEtown, N.C. - A Parktown woman was taken to a hospital with a bullet going through her head early Friday at St. Mary's Hospital, said N.C. Hospital Chief Robert White. Deputies visited the woman, 73-year-old Austin Jones, in a nearby Parktown apartment complex and heard a bullet going through her head, White said in the news release. The bullet hit Jones repeatedly and damaged the rest of her leg, White said. Jones repeatedly shot her while she was wearing a hammer, he said. \"I hear the woman right now say, shots going through her head right in her face, and it's disheartening,\" White said. Another neighbor, Jennifer Webb, said she heard shots going through the woman's head as the man was coming face to face with her family. \"The shots went through her head down the neck. Now he's shot her repeatedly,\" Webb said. Deputies could not determine whether any shots were fired through the woman's nexus at the scene. Jones' right hand was shot through his neck, and both legs were damaged, Webb said. Deputies yelled at Jones, telling him to jump up and down by saying the woman's leg was broken, but they could hear him being shot repeatedly at that point. \"There were no bullets or shots through his head at that point so that he was coming face to face-to-face with anyone when he was shot from behind,\" Jones' sister-in-law, Jennifer Smith told KPRY in a phone interview. \"He was shot repeatedly. It was like he was a criminal,\" Smith said. Jones was taken from hospital in an apartment complex at 2500 S. Latlana Ave. She was taken to Flint General Hospital at about 6:30 p.m., where she was hospitalized in stable condition. They found her with a handgun and a small bullet through her elbow, Smith said. Flint police spokeswoman Jennifer Shaw said that they didn't know the mass shooter who shot Jones with the gun. \"This was a black woman who was wearing a hammer with a bullet going through her head,\" she said. A picture of Jones' right hand, which remains intact, has been uploaded to social media. Another neighbor, Loencing Jones, said she saw a white woman was walking near the home when the shooting occurred. \"It was just a bunch of shots fired through her elbow or leg,\" she said. Loencing Jones said deputies helped get the woman taken home to St. Mary General Hospital, but didn't confirm whether the shots were fired. Another neighbor, Mario Murphy, said she heard Jones being shot repeatedly as her family and son were walking. Murphy said eyewitnesses could not determine who Jones was shooting. \"He was in stable condition,\" she said. \"If he ever was going to do it, I didn't want to see him again. He was never going to come face to face with anyone else. He was trying to do something horrible.\" Contributing: A 29-year-old boy was critically injured in another shooting at a mid-night party biking session on Tuesday evening in East Rockville, Dallas Police Department said Tuesday A 29-year-old boy was critically injured in another shooting at a mid-night party biking session on Tuesday afternoon in East Rockville, the Dallas Police Department said Tuesday When the shooting happened at a home on the 1200 block of Sullivan Street, a 22-year-old boy was struck and killed. His son suffered multiple injuries in the shooting, according to his mother. He had one round trickled through his head when he was struck and his son was taken to a nearby hospital, the mother said. He had one round trickled and he was taken to a nearby hospital immediately, according to his mother. It was less than five minutes before the Dallas Police Department arrived at a home on Flint Street at about 8:40 a.m. and found someone walking gunman at a scene on the corner of Orange Road, about three blocks east of the home, according to the mother. He was rushed to a nearby hospital where he suffered multiple injuries. The shooting began at 6 a.m.. The suspect fled the scene several times before officers arrived. When officers arrived, he \"visibly began to take out his weapons and began to take a gun away from the victim and fired multiple rounds through his head,\" said police spokesman Bruce Grazero before leaving. N/A The shooting happened in the parking lot of the 1200 block of Sullivan Street, and the victim was sitting with a rifle in his hand, Grazero said."
