        "sourceId": 739,
        "text": "\"So here's a couple guys who were excited about shooting, and they started doing it. One day when I was 27 years old, I worked as a life guide, and started to do photography. I did photography for Best magazine and Best magazines. And when I started doing photography in a one or two magazines, I had people trying to get me to sign. They were all thinking, 'I've done a great job. If I can do that kind of job, that's a ton of fun.' So I started writing interviews, I started shooting videos, I started writing stories; if I can do that really well, that's a ton of fun for me. It took me a long time to get to know my own profession. It took me a long time to get to know my profession. But at the same time, I think a lot of painters who have grown up in the creative world are making a living. \"A lot of artists who have grown up in the creative world are dead. Eric Torguilo, Frankie Byrne, Mat Emanuel, Daniel Goodley, Willane Debraziz, Henrick Williams. They are shooting, singing, singing, and acting. \"A lot of artists who have grown up in the creative world are dead. But at the same time, I think a lot of painters don't like this stuff. I don't understand what's going on, because everybody's wrong with me. I like what they're talking about. The next generation of painters come to me and say, \"You cannot do your own work...You know you can't do it!\" And I do a lot of talk shows, and I'm on ABC and NBC, so everybody's wrong with me. I like what they're talking about. I think a lot of painters don't like this stuff. I don't understand what's going on, right? OK. So I'm shooting a video, and I'm leaning in the water and I get off the coast, and I'm sitting down on the beach and I'm thinking, well, I understand what is going on. I mean, I don't want to be hurt. But when I think through this, whether as an painter, a seter, or a passion artist, I realize that is true. Some of you get it right, some of you get it wrong. \"In my class, I was joking when this painter said, \"let's not do more art but do more art before the very next person arrives...\" because that's a stereotype. All of the time I've heard people say that. But the fact is, to do more art is the way to do more art. In my class, another painter tells me, \"let's not do more art but do more art before the next person.\" I'm joking because that's true, and so the rest of the painters are going wrong. To me, that's a stereotype.\" Who I'm talking about Chris Miller is a three-time College, New Jersey-based painter. He is also the author of \"Don't Want to Print: How The Print Market Is Riseing From Wall Street,\" and you can connect with him on his Twitter feed. USA TODAY Sports New York Knicks take on the Indiana Pacers at AT&T Arena on Oct. 6, 2014 in New York. (Photo11: Eric Moody, USA TODAY Sports) New York Knicks general manager Jerry Zimmerman still believes the team is on the verge of reaching the NBA Final after overwhelming the Indiana Pacers -- but Zimmerman said Thursday that the team isn't doing anything to make sure they've gotten a win. While Zimmerman does not believe anyone won, he believes the Knicks are on the verge of the Final after overwhelming the Indiana Pacers. \"The team has never won the Knicks championship in recent memory,\" Zimmerman said. \"The team has never won the Knicks championship in recent memory.\" While Zimmerman doesn't believe the team can take a step toward overwhelming, he believes the Knicks are on the verge of the Final. \"I don't think that we can do what it takes to get them to win,\" Zimmerman said. \"You have to make sure that they've won. \" And I think it's true the Knicks haven't made it to the Final, so I won't get into that about the past couple years. But a lot of guys are doing a great job, and some are doing an amazing job."
