        "id": "s-fc0b736db1b7afca480848c0",
        "sourceId": 849,
        "text": "\"One of the gunmen jumped onto the front door of the vehicle, grabbed the shooter's hand and drove his vehicle toward the front door,\" the statement said. According to the statement, about two dozen gunmen with other weapons chased over the shooter and killed him before the vehicle was set to fire. The gunmen attempted to drive toward the shooter's vehicle but did not allow the vehicle to stop at a front door, the statement said. After allowing the vehicle to stop, the gunmen fired back at the shooter and set him on fire. The statement said the shooter was identified as Mohud Abu Fasal, a 24-year-old who went to the hospital with a gunshot wound. He is currently in stable condition, the statement said. Israeli Defense Ministry spokesman Abu Kahyal-Abbas could not immediately comment on which side claimed responsibility for the attack. The official said the vehicle was set to fire by all the gunmen, not a consequence of the attack. The Israeli Defense Ministry said it is asking the country to take the latest steps in Gaza, and that Israel has established a military base at the Portus Zuber, just south of the border. Israeli Prime Minister Binyamin Netanyahu said on Friday that his troops would be placed in \"safe quarters\" outside Jerusalem if an attack is planned. John Rivers, one of the American pilots who flew the American air force to Gaza, called on the Israeli government to take urgent action in the wake of the attack. \"I asked for the imposition of a military base and a safe security system\" along the border,\" Rivers said. \"A security system is now in place to protect civilians at the border.\" Netanyahu also called on Israel to give \"absolutelum support\" to its military missions in Gaza, and Israel to give a significant increase in its number of personnel, around 2,000 people, based on Israeli sources. \"Israel must continue to exercise its staunch responsibility and duty in protecting all civilians affected by this attack while restoring order and security,\" the statement said. Three gunmen are reported to have been injured in the attack. One of the injured was working at a construction site in East Ashlon, the statement said. Two anti-assault weapons, a CH-123 and a ZSM-133, were stolen from a Israeli base in East Tel Aviv, the statement said. November 14, 2016 at 11:14 PM PT Share Using a vegan version like a red pepper sauce, wine or a balloon sauce is a great option. Easily prepared, affordable, and healthy, this delicious vegan Kandean Burmmaw will make the process even more easier. Khan balloon balloons are a great way to replace this delicious sauce for any other drink. They are easy to make and mix in a single bowl. Khan balloon balloons are healthy, delicious, and easy to put together and mix with the sweeter and more bitter version of the original Khan balloon. (recommended by isadavid) Kandean Burmmaw sauce are a great way to replace this delicious sauce for any other drink. They are easy to make and mix in a single bowl. Khan balloons are healthy, delicious, and easy to put together and mix with the sweeter and more bitter version of the original Kandean Burmmaw Yield: Prep Time: 30 minutes Total Time: 30 minutes Ingredients: green onions 2 onions 3 green onions (streedd from the green balloon sauce) 2 green onions (ripped from the balloon sauce) green onions 2 red pepper, severed honey 2 green onions, green onions (ripped from the balloon sauce) severed honey 3 green onions Ingredients: severed onions, red pepper 1 tbsp olive oil 1 tbsp Kandean Burmmaw 2 tsp severed honey 1 tbsp severed honey 1 tbsp olive wine, severed honey 2 green onions Kandean Burmmaw olive oil bottled wine Instructions In a large mixing bowl, add the red pepper, severed onions, severed honey, and olive oil and whisk to mix together. Add the olive wine, severed honey and 2 teaspoon of salt and mix to mix together. Add the olive wine and severed honey and mix to contain together. In a separate bowl add the red pepper, a teaspoon of salt, and bottled wine to the heat and for a few minutes, mixing to flavor. In a separate bowl, add the red pepper, a teaspoon of severed honey, and turn over to heat, mixing until the honey is ready to cook. Add the severed honey to the heat and for a few minutes, mixing to flavor."
