        "id": "s-e3b82d3c6cc6a8e1e0b5abfc",
        "sourceId": 448,
        "text": "I’m so grateful to have these guys here. We recently met Lise Kugl, and also really met Me and Derek, and I loved it too. They did a fantastic job in bringing this group to the mainstream, and it’s been heartbreaking to finally be able to follow these guys on Facebook, Instagram, and the various channels I belong to. I’m always going to have to think back to the day I saw this group, and it’s so great to look back and see what we’re doing. We did a lot of media work with this group last week, so a lot of the work didn’t end up the same way. I spent a lot of time just talking to people and telling their stories about our work, our lives, and our projects. We spent the next couple of days doing a really good training camp, where my husband and I got to get back on the road for the first time. I loved this camp, and it was heartbreaking to see them all out there. Just knowing their work, and enjoying their time off made it feel such a privilege, and to know these guys so well. It’s been great. I’m always looking forward talking to people. I’m really excited to be able to meet them, and I’m really enjoying the camp we’re going on together. This camp is a great venue for anyone who is looking to be an elite band or supporting player. Of course, you’re the only person that this group listens to. I’m hoping that I’ll have more time to listen, and maybe even participate in these camp events in London. You’ve definitely welcomed these guys here. Why do your members sound so similar to you, and because these guys sound so similar to you? Jeanka: It’s been absolutely amazing. John Collins has done a fantastic job inbringing us all together. But I also love his singing and just getting on the cue of the guitar and getting into the gimmick and trying to see what he can do with this group. I mean, it’s really heartbreaking, too for me, because the members of this group have been hanging around so long. Jack Teleto! Teleto: I know that I’m older than most of these singers, but pursuit my goals has always been high in the sky for me. Whether you have a good job, or not meeting what you promise, you never seem to miss your opportunity. Tell me about Nick Williamson when he said this: “I ampursuing my goals all the time as a singer. Whether you like it or not, people like to talk about making sure you meet your expectations. I want to do everything that’s necessary in order to achieve that. Even right now, when I can’t do what I’m supposed to do, all I want to do is fix it. My bar for achievement is very high.” One of my favorite songs, though, was when you passed. I believe that music honors a songwriter’s achievement, but if they aren’t doing it in the way they’re supposed, I try to do it in that way. Teleto: I feel like you were recording your song when you passed away. Nick Williamson recorded some of your favorite songs when you passed. Jeanka: That’s awesome. Teleto: I also love recording some of my favorite songs. I’ve listened mostly to line-ups over the years. I typically  listen to very different styles of guitar—basic guitar, bass guitar, bass guitar, electro guitar, light and cloud guitar, bass guitar, and bass guitar, etc. Teleto: Last year, you were touring with Lise Jarden at the annual London Guitar Festival. What are some of your favorite moments from your time with him? Nick Williamson: We’d never been together before. We’ve been working together for a few years. I recorded my first song, One Great Day, in May, and I was sitting next to his table, laughing and talking to him so much. It was so fun. Teleto: Since you passed, you’ve managed to release a bunch of new albums once again. Jeanka: Over the last few days, he’s released a bunch of albums—one single, which I was overwhelmed with. It’s really exciting that other songs I recorded have come out here. I’ve managed to put together one of the most liberated bands I’ve ever done. It’s true that I’ve never been able to go that far, but I’ve really mastered the big challenge that I’m going through: building a powerful band and following. It’s awesome, and I love having the opportunity to do it all for myself."
